# play.poki2.online — Cloudflare Pages redirects
#
# TWO HARD LIMITS ON THIS FILE. Both are silent, and both were measured on
# 2026-11-06 by deploying probe builds and reading the responses.
#
# 1. Pages applies ONLY the first 100 redirect declarations in this file.
#    Everything from declaration #101 onward is dropped — no warning, no
#    error, nothing in the build log. The request just 404s.
#    Evidence: /games/geodash is declaration #100 and answers 301 in
#    production, /games/getaway-shootout is declaration #102 and answers
#    404. A probe build that placed the same rule at declaration #100 and at
#    #106 reproduced exactly that cut. Keep every rule that must work inside
#    the first 100 declarations.
#
# 2. Only 301/302/303/307/308 are supported. Any other status code — 410 in
#    particular — is ignored, and the rule does nothing: the request falls
#    through to the static asset layer.
#    Evidence: the old "/ads.txt / 410" rule sat at declaration #3 and
#    /ads.txt still answered 200 with the live file.
#
# Rule order matters: Pages applies the first matching rule, and static
# rules are meant to come before dynamic (splat) ones.
#
# The 442-rule /games/<slug> -> /game/<c>/<slug>/ table was removed on
# 2026-11-06. It was a copy of the apex table; it pushed every hand-written
# rule past declaration #100, where it died silently; and it had no
# audience at all: Google answers "URL is unknown to Google" for every
# play.poki2.online/games/* URL, and no page on either host links to that
# path. The apex still serves the same legacy shape from its redirect
# worker (poki2.online/games/* -> play.poki2.online/game/<c>/<slug>/), and
# that covers the URLs which ever really existed.
#
# Note: no SPA fallback — every real route is a static file; unknown paths
# must return 404.html (a 200-rewrite to index.html would create soft-404
# duplicate content and hurt GSC indexing).

# The /2-player-games/ URL experiment was rolled back on 2026-11-04 — the
# "poki 2 player games" hub lives on the apex host (https://poki2.online/
# 2-player-games) and this tag keeps its neutral /tag/multiplayer/ URL.
# Reverse 301 so the briefly-live URL's signals return to the tag page.
# Query strings (?page=N) are appended by the client after the redirect.
/2-player-games  /tag/multiplayer/  301
/2-player-games/ /tag/multiplayer/  301

# /tag/classic/ deleted 2026-11-04 (user call): 38 mostly-single-player games
# under a "classic" umbrella with a thin, boilerplate-heavy page. 301 to the
# home so the URL's signals are not stranded on a 404.
/tag/classic  /  301
/tag/classic/ /  301

# /omica is migration debris (2026-11-06). A flat game slug with no page
# behind it: the shard layout used o.poki2.online/omica/ and the current one
# uses /game/o/omica/, and neither exists — the catalogue has om-bounce and
# ojelloonline under /game/o/, and category == slug[0] for all 221 games, so
# /game/o/omica/ would have been the URL if the game existed. It appears in
# no sitemap, no page links to it, and Google answers "URL is unknown to
# Google" for it.
# 301 to the catalogue home rather than 410: Pages ignores 410 (limit 2
# above), so a 410 rule would leave the URL answering 404 — and a 404
# sampled by the property's coverage validation is exactly what made the
# 2026-11-04 "Crawled - currently not indexed" validation fail.
/omica  /  301

# Legacy path prefixes from the pre-migration structure.
/play/*       /  301
/category/*   /  301

# /blog/* belongs to the apex host — the articles live at
# poki2.online/blog/<slug> and always did (the apex repo's very first commit
# already carried src/content/blog/). A /blog/ path arriving on this host is
# a cross-host leak from the poki2.online -> play.poki2.online migration, so
# it goes back to the host that owns it: 301, not 410, because the
# destination is a real page and the correct answer to "this URL is on the
# wrong host" is to send it home.
# The apex property's "Crawled - currently not indexed" validation sampled
# play.poki2.online/blog/best-shooting-browser-games, it 404'd, and the
# validation could not pass.
/blog/*  https://poki2.online/blog/:splat  301
